          "note": "Sect. 4.2, Fig. 3 and conclusions: the strong isotropic ν₁ (A₁) band near 2916 cm⁻¹, a Q branch that is unresolved at the 0.3 cm⁻¹ apparatus width; spontaneous Raman of ¹²CH₄ in a heated gas cell at low density (about one amagat, below 1 atm to avoid line mixing), 4 W argon-ion laser, room temperature to 900 K. The stimulated Raman spectrum at 0.08 bar and 300 K (Fig. 8) resolves that Q branch into lines between about 2916.5 and 2918 cm⁻¹, read off the figure. From 400 K on, hot bands ν₁+nνᵢ−nνᵢ fill 2900–2920 cm⁻¹ (ν₁+ν₄−ν₄ at 2913 cm⁻¹, Fig. 10), which is what makes the band a thermometer. ν₁ is in Fermi resonance with 2ν₂ and 2ν₄ and in Dennison resonance with ν₂+ν₄. Laser line assumed, not reported: the paper names only a 4 W argon-ion laser, and 515 nm is its strongest green line."
