          "measured_on": [
            "ag_au_film"
          ],
          "technique": "seiras",
          "medium": "liquid",
          "form": "adsorbed",
          "note": "Fig. 2e, f: deconvolved spectra of the Ag film during CO₂ reduction, E(c) = −1.1 V vs. RHE, at 188.3 s and 526.7 s. A broad shoulder from about 1650 to 1730 cm⁻¹ under −0.2 V pulses is read as formate and hollow-site CO overlapping, and the CO part is fitted at 1704 and 1719. The main text hedges it (\"likely\"); the CO-dosed sweep labels the same species. Their calculation puts hollow CO far higher, which they put down to the large overpotential and the missing Stark slope. That \"hollow\" on Ag(111) means this three-fold band is this collection’s assumption; Fig. S20c draws the CO in a hollow."
        },
