      "short": "ν(CO)/Mⁿ⁺",
      "description": "Linear CO adsorbed on a Lewis-acidic cation site rather than a reduced metal atom. Markedly less metal→CO π-backdonation than on a metallic surface, blue-shifting ν(CO) above the free-gas value (2143 cm⁻¹) rather than below it — the opposite direction from every metallic-surface CO band in this dataset. Position correlates with the cation's formal charge and Lewis acidity, making this band a widely used spectroscopic probe of acid-site strength and oxidation state; the same ¹³CO isotope-shift check used for metallic sites applies here too.",
