          "note": "Table 1 and Sect. 3.1.3 (Cu-ZSM-5, Si/Al 25 and 1.01 wt% Cu, ion-exchanged from copper acetate, calcined at 673 K, reduced in 5 kPa CO at 473 K and evacuated; self-supporting pellet, transmission, 2 cm⁻¹; CO at 100 K, and low coverage at ambient temperature, SI Fig. S2 not read here): Cu⁺–CO resolved into three families of dry Cu⁺. 2158 cm⁻¹ on the principal cationic sites (type II); a shoulder at 2166 on a minor, more electrophilic family that water covers first (type I), backed by a second νₛ dicarbonyl component at 2182; and 2141 at higher coverage on Cu⁺ not in cationic positions, more highly coordinated, from an oxide-like phase (type III). Dosed at 100 K the principal band appears at 2157. The water-coordinated sites are a claim of their own."
        },
