          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": [
            "direct-dosing"
          ],
          "note": "Sect. 3.2.1 and Table 1, type IV (same Cu-ZSM-5 with water: added to a CO-precovered sample, or adsorbed and evacuated at ambient temperature before CO at 100 K; SI Figs. S4 and S5 not read here): mixed aqua-carbonyls. Water moves the 2158 cm⁻¹ band to 2132, Cu⁺(H₂O)₂CO; lowering the water pressure gives 2139, Cu⁺(H₂O)(CO), and long evacuation returns 2158. The paper reads the lower frequency as a weaker σ and electrostatic bond, the π back-bond barely changed since the integrated intensity hardly moves. 2139 nearly coincides with CO on oxide-like Cu⁺ at 2141."
        },
