          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "adsorbed",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Section 2.3.2, p. 95 of a monograph, with no single measurement behind it, so no position is recorded here. A low-frequency band between 2100 and 2130 cm⁻¹ has been assigned by several authors to Mⁿ⁺···OC adducts, CO bound through the oxygen lone pair rather than the carbon, which shifts the stretch down where the ordinary orientation shifts it up. The book records an isomerisation equilibrium between the two orientations on NaZSM-5, Z-Na···CO against Z-Na⁺···OC, with an enthalpy of 3.8 kJ mol⁻¹, so on an alkali cation the two coexist rather than one of them winning. A summary rather than one measurement; the experiments it draws on adsorb CO on samples held under the probe gas, so gas is this collection’s reading."
