      "atoms": "C-O",
      "wn_start": 2020,
      "wn_end": 2160,
      "short": "νₐₛ(CO) gem-M⁺(CO)₂",
      "description": "Asymmetric ν(CO) component of a geminal dicarbonyl species: two linear CO ligands bound to a single isolated cationic metal center, stretching out of phase (one lengthens as the other shortens). The symmetric/asymmetric pair appearing together, rather than a single linear-CO band, is itself diagnostic of an atomically dispersed cationic site — a single metal atom isolated enough to bind two CO molecules at once. The symmetric component lies above the antisymmetric one, and the splitting depends on the cation: 29 cm⁻¹ for Cu⁺(CO)₂ in ZSM-5, about 70 for Rh⁺(CO)₂. The firm test of a geminal pair is a ¹²CO/¹³CO mixture: two ligands coupled on one cation give mixed-isotope bands that two neighbouring monocarbonyls cannot.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 105,
          "key": "Zdravkova.SurprisingCoordinationChemistry.2015",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "adsorbed",
          "wn": 2151,
          "measured_on": [
            "cu_1p",
            "cu_zsm5"
          ],
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": [
            "isotope-labeling",
            "direct-dosing"
          ],
          "note": "Sect. 3.1.3 (Cu-ZSM-5, Si/Al 25 and 1.01 wt% Cu, ion-exchanged from copper acetate, calcined at 673 K, reduced in 5 kPa CO at 473 K and evacuated; self-supporting pellet, transmission, 2 cm⁻¹): CO dosed at 100 K in increasing amounts first gives Cu⁺–CO at 2157 cm⁻¹, then the Cu⁺(CO)₂ dicarbonyl, νₐₛ at 2151 with νₛ at 2180. Under gas-phase CO much of it goes on to the tricarbonyl (2191, 2167 cm⁻¹); evacuation at 100 K removes the tricarbonyl and leaves the dicarbonyl. The geminal structure rests on Sect. 3.3.1: the same pair forms when NO is dosed onto a sample precovered with equal ¹²CO and ¹³CO, and the mixed-isotope bands match a force-field calculation; those positions are their own bands. Corrected: this note once described that test as adsorbing the isotopic mixture alone."
        }
      ],
      "tags": ["site-sensitive"],
      "vibration_modes": ["co_geminal_stretch_asymmetric"]
