          "note": "Table 3 and Fig. 3B, 30 bar. CZ, a coprecipitated Cu/ZnO with Cu:Zn 2.1:1, diluted to 8 wt% in KBr and activated in H₂ at 513 K; 3H₂/CO₂ at 20 NmL min⁻¹, 513 K, 4 cm⁻¹, 64 scans. ν(C=O) at 1759 cm⁻¹, assigned either to formyl *HCO or to *HCOOH held by a weak hydrogen bond, the small red shift from gaseous HC(=O)OH at 1776 cm⁻¹ being the argument for the latter. One of four bands (1759, 1691, 1457 and 1398 cm⁻¹) whose intensity rises with the GHSV and with the methanol in the outlet gas, which is this paper’s criterion for a true intermediate rather than a spectator. Absent under a 2H₂/CO feed, where no adsorbate could be identified between 2400 and 2000 cm⁻¹ at all."
