      "short": "ν(C=O) HCOOH*",
      "description": "C=O stretch of formic acid adsorbed without losing its proton. It is the one band that tells molecular HCOOH* from the formate it becomes: formate has no localised carbonyl, its two C-O bonds being equivalent, so nothing of its own absorbs here. An absorption in this window after dosing formic acid therefore means the acid did not fully dissociate, and its disappearance on warming tracks the deprotonation. It sits among the surface carbonyl and carbonate bands, which is the standing ambiguity where the acid was not deliberately dosed.",
