          "tags": ["direct-dosing"],
          "note": "Table 1 and Fig. 6b, 6f (IRRAS, UHV, room temperature): a band absent from the group's earlier unpolarized work, strong in s-polarized light and much weaker in p, which puts the C=O bond tilted rather than flat. DFT for a monodentate molecular species gives 1721 cm⁻¹. It is the paper's evidence that formic acid adsorbs monodentate and undissociated alongside the formate on this facet. Nothing equivalent appears on Fe₃O₄(001) at room temperature, where a 1700 cm⁻¹ band was seen only at 190 K in earlier work."
        }
