          "note": "Fig. 4b (3 wt% Pt/CeO₂ reduced in 10% H₂ at 300 °C; 200 °C, 1 bar, H₂/CO₂ = 4 in He; external background under He): ν(CH) of formate at 2846 cm⁻¹, the lower member of the doublet the paper calls a Fermi resonance, with 2945 cm⁻¹ above it. Under ¹³CO₂ the pair moves to 2830 and 2910 cm⁻¹, which no ¹³C formate band here records yet. Formate exchanges more slowly than CO(g) at every position (Fig. 5), so the paper rules the formate route out as the main one at 200 °C, while noting it speeds up markedly at 250 °C (Fig. S7, not read here). Corrected: this row once carried 2910 cm⁻¹, the ¹³C position of the upper member, as the ¹²C ν(CH)."
