          "technique": "drifts",
          "note": "Figs. 4a and 4c (steady state, 10 bar), 5b (H₂/D₂ switching, 10 bar) and 7a (He+CO₂ against H₂+He, 20 bar): operando DRIFTS of CuZn/SiO₂, 230 °C, H₂/CO₂ = 3, 10 NmL min⁻¹, after H₂ at 300 °C. Bidentate formate on Cu at 2856 cm⁻¹ in the steady-state spectra, the first and most abundant surface species, appearing together with the Zn²⁺-bound formate; 2850 in the MCR-resolved component spectra of both transients. It exchanges to κ²-DCOO* at 2167 cm⁻¹ within the 10 s time resolution, so formate formation is not rate-limiting, and in the transient it falls as CO* at 2113 cm⁻¹ rises, which the authors read as formate decomposing to CO on Cu. The 2850 is an MCR component maximum, not a raw peak."
