          "note": "H₂-TPSR after CO₂ adsorption on precipitated Ga₂O₃ (Fig. S13 inset and Table S2; the same band appears in Fig. 5a under CO₂/H₂ = 1:3, and at 2898 cm⁻¹ in Fig. 4c, where CO₂ is dosed onto a pre-formed Ga-H surface at 200 °C). Weak beside the 1581 cm⁻¹ OCO band of the same formate: on this oxide the C-H stretch is a minor feature, which is why it is easy to miss on Ga-containing catalysts. Fig. 4c is the cleanest of the three, since there the formate can only have come from the hydride."
