          "tags": [],
          "note": "Fig. 1A and Table 1 (operando DRIFTS, 6 wt% Cu/ZrO₂, 220 °C, 3 bar, 20 % CO₂ + 60 % H₂ in He, steady state, background the reduced sample under H₂): ν(CH) of formate on the zirconia at 2873 cm⁻¹, with νₐₛ(OCO) at 1575 and a third band at 1380. Sodium-formate standards dry-impregnated on Cu-free zirconia give the same position and band shape (Fig. 1B), which is what makes the quantification possible; of the paper's two calibration bands this is the more accurate, because the C–H bond is not the part touching the surface (Fig. 1C). Two kinetically distinct zirconia formates share it, a fast one near the copper interface and a slow one away from it, and their spectra differ only in a slight shift of the maxima."
