          "note": "Figs. 6a to 6c (operando DRIFTS, 30ZnHfOₓ, 320 °C, 20 bar, switching 20 vol% CO₂ → 80 vol% H₂ → H₂:CO₂:N₂ = 3:1:1, all in N₂): the dominant formate band, which the paper calls ν(C=O). It appears the instant H₂ replaces CO₂ and fades as methoxy grows; re-admitting CO₂ restores it at once while methoxy falls, the formate-methoxy pathway read straight off the spectra. The site is the paper's postulate: the formate and methoxy bands on 30ZnHfOₓ sit 4 to 5 cm⁻¹ below those on HfO₂ and between the two single oxides (Fig. 8e), which it reads as stabilisation at a Zn–Vₒ–Hf motif. Fig. S49 repeats the sequence on 20ZnHfOₓ with the same result; its caption repeats Fig. 6's tracking positions word for word, so it is not recorded as a separate 20ZnHfOₓ position."
