      "short": "νₐₛ(OCO) m-HCOO*",
      "description": "Asymmetric OCO stretch of formate bound through one oxygen. With the other oxygen free the mode is close to a C=O stretch, and papers often name it that. It lies above the 1515 to 1650 cm⁻¹ of bridging and chelating formate because the two C-O bonds no longer share the bond order equally, and that gap is what identifies the geometry. It overlaps carbonyls, hollow-site CO and the water bend, so a lone band here needs a second argument (the symmetric partner, a calculation, isotope substitution) before it is read as formate.",
