            1674,
            1671,
            1669
          ],
          "measured_on": [
            "ag_au_film"
          ],
          "technique": "seiras",
          "medium": "liquid",
          "form": "adsorbed",
          "note": "Fig. 2e to g: Ag film in CO₂-saturated 0.1 M CsHCO₃, pulsed at E(c) = −1.1 V and E(a) = −0.2 V vs. RHE. A peak near 1674 cm⁻¹ appears throughout these pulses and is far stronger than under static or +0.7 V pulsed electrolysis: 1674 and 1671 in the deconvolved cathodic spectra (188.3 s, 526.7 s), about 1669 during the −0.2 V period itself (191.6 s), where it rivals bridged CO. The authors assign it to the C=O stretch of monodentate formate, *OCHO(M), from a calculation on Ag(111) and a grand canonical DFT estimate that formate is favoured over adsorbed H at −0.2 V, and tie it to the higher formate yield under −0.2 V pulses. It overlaps the hollow-CO shoulder."
        },
        {
          "id": 405,
          "key": "Ye.MolecularLevelInsights.2024",
          "medium": "vacuum",
          "form": "adsorbed",
          "wn": 1657,
          "measured_on": [
            "ag_111"
          ],
          "technique": "computational",
          "note": "Fig. 2d, with coordinates in Supplementary Data 1 (not read): spin-polarised DFT, RPBE with D3 dispersion in VASP, a three-layer 3 × 3 Ag(111) slab, frequencies by finite differences in ASE (±0.005 Å). The applied potential is left out of the frequency calculation, which the authors do for simplicity, so this is a zero-field value set against Stark-shifted measurements. Monodentate formate’s C=O stretch calculated at 1657 cm⁻¹, against 1680 to 1670 measured. The slab carries 15 Å of vacuum and the frequency calculation no solvent."
        },
        {
          "id": 412,
          "key": "Ye.MolecularLevelInsights.2024",
