    // SURFACE METHOXY (CH₃O*)
    // Methanol precursor — bonds via O to surface cations on a wide variety of
    // oxide and oxide-supported catalysts (TiO₂, ZrO₂, SiO₂, Ga₂O₃, ZnO, Cu-based
    // systems, ...). On most oxide supports CH₃O* exists in two adsorption
    // geometries diagnostically distinguished by ν(C-O): monodentate (bonded
    // via O to a single cation) above ~1100 cm⁻¹ and bidentate (bridging two
    // cations or at a bridging-O vacancy) below ~1100 cm⁻¹ (Hussein 1991, Wu 2000).
    // CH₃ stretching/bending modes are essentially insensitive to the geometry
    // but are sensitive to the cation identity / local environment: e.g. on Cu/SiO₂
    // νₐₛ is ~2926 cm⁻¹ but shifts to ~2919 cm⁻¹ on Ga-promoted Cu (Cu⁺ site at
    // Cu–Ga₂O₃ interface; Gómez 2024). On Zr-rich supports CH₃O* is typically
    // Zr-OCH₃ with ν(C-O) at ~1150 cm⁻¹ (Al Abdulghani 2025).
    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
