      "description": "Methoxy CH₃ asymmetric stretch, one C-H bond moving out of phase with the other two. It tracks νₛ(CH₃) below, so a shift in both is a sign that the binding environment itself has changed. Coadsorbed methanol sits a little higher and is easily read as the same species. Silica is the outlier among supports: methoxy grafted as Si-O-CH₃ absorbs near 2955 to 2960 cm⁻¹, some 30 cm⁻¹ above the same mode on Cu.",
