          "technique": "drifts",
          "tags": ["direct-dosing"],
          "note": "Fig. S16a and Table S5 (operando DRIFTS, 10% CH₃OH/Ar at 20 mL min⁻¹, 220 °C, atmospheric pressure, then swept with Ar): νₐₛ(CH₃) of the methoxy left after dosing methanol on Cu/SiO₂ and removing the physisorbed layer. This is the reference experiment that verifies the methoxy attribution under reaction. It sits 28 cm⁻¹ above the band measured under CO₂ and H₂ on the same catalyst, which the paper does not comment on; the value is close to where methoxy grafted onto silica is usually reported."
