          "technique": "drifts",
          "note": "Figs. 4a and 4c (steady state, 10 bar), 5b (H₂/D₂ switching, 10 bar) and 7a (He+CO₂ against H₂+He, 20 bar): CuZn/SiO₂, 230 °C, H₂/CO₂ = 3, 10 NmL min⁻¹, after H₂ at 300 °C. νₐₛ(CH₃) of methoxy on the silica at 2958 cm⁻¹, 2956 in the transient. Methoxy grafted to the silica (Si-O-CH₃), not to Cu or the promoter: it builds up slowly and exchanges over minutes to hours under D₂. Fig. S14 splits it into a reactive pool near the Cu/Zn²⁺ interface and a slow spectator pool on remote silica; hydrogenating or desorbing the reactive pool is the rate-limiting step (KIE 2.78)."
