      "description": "Methoxy CH₃ symmetric stretch (CH₃O*), shifting in tandem with νₐₛ(CH₃) above. Often appears as a close shoulder pair with a coadsorbed methanol band sitting a little higher in frequency. Silica-grafted methoxy is the extreme case, ~2856–2859 cm⁻¹, some 40 cm⁻¹ above the same mode on Cu — high enough that it lands directly on formate's own ν(CH) on metallic Cu (the low end of ν(CH) HCOO*). On a silica-supported Cu catalyst the two are effectively coincident and cannot be separated by position alone.",
