      "description": "O-D stretch of O-deuterated methanol, the hydroxyl counterpart of ν(OH) MeOH nearly 1000 cm⁻¹ lower. Drawn as the full R to P envelope, since all three branches sit inside 40 cm⁻¹. The point of moving the band here is escape: methanol's O-H stretch is the one most easily lost under support hydroxyls and adsorbed water. The escape is only partial, because the new position collides with the C-H stretching region instead.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 270,
          "key": "Falk.InfraredSpectraMethanol.1961",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "wn": [2720, 2745, 2705],
          "note": "Table II, CH₃OD vapour in a 10-cm cell at 80 mmHg and room temperature: ν(OD) Q 2720 cm⁻¹, R 2745, P 2705. Against Table I's ν(OH) Q at 3687 cm⁻¹ this is Δν(OH→OD) = −967 cm⁻¹, close to the harmonic √2 expectation for an X-H bond and the basis for the attribution.",
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": []
        },
        {
          "id": 271,
          "key": "Dinu.HowVibrationalNotations.2024",
          "medium": "matrix",
          "form": "free",
          "wn": 2721.7,
          "note": "Table 3, ν₁(A′) νOD of CH₃OD in solid neon at 6 K; 2704.8 cm⁻¹ in argon, against 2717.6 cm⁻¹ in the gas phase. Deuterating the hydroxyl leaves the methyl bands almost where they were, which is what makes it the clean way to separate O-H from C-H features.",
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": []
        },
        {
          "id": 272,
          "key": "Dinu.HowVibrationalNotations.2024",
          "medium": "matrix",
          "form": "free",
          "wn": 2723.0,
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Table 3, ν₁(A′) νOD of the fully deuterated CD₃OD in solid neon at 6 K; 2705.3 cm⁻¹ in argon. It sits 1.3 cm⁻¹ from the same mode in CH₃OD, which is the point: the O-D stretch does not care whether the methyl group is deuterated, so both are recorded on this one band."
        },
        {
          "id": 273,
          "key": "Falk.InfraredSpectraMethanol.1961",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "wn": 2724,
          "note": "Table IV, CD₃OD vapour: Q branch of the O-D stretch at 2724 cm⁻¹, R 2746 and P 2708 cm⁻¹. Within 4 cm⁻¹ of the same mode in CH₃OD (Table II, 2720 cm⁻¹), which is the vapour-phase version of the point that the O-D stretch does not care whether the methyl group is deuterated.",
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": []
        }
      ],
