      "short": "ν(CH) in-plane MeOH",
      "description": "The C-H stretch of methanol's in-plane hydrogen, the one lying in the C-O-H plane: 78% of the motion is on that single bond, the rest shared by the out-of-plane pair moving together. The older tables call it a symmetric methyl stretch, which is also what they call ν₃ 150 cm⁻¹ lower, and that duplicate name is why this region reads as ambiguous (see the vibration-modes page). It sits close enough to the O-H stretch's low-wavenumber tail that the two can blur together in a broad surface spectrum.",
