          "laser_nm": 515,
          "wn": 2996,
          "technique": "raman",
          "tags": ["undissociated"],
          "note": "Table 2, vapour column of a Raman study recording vapour, liquid and argon-matrix methanol on one instrument, 515 nm, 3 W at the sample for the vapour cell. Assigned there as ν₂ and called a CH₃ asymmetric stretch; the index matches this band, the name is the older convention that Dinu's notation study replaces, since the motion is 78% the in-plane C-H bond rather than any asymmetric combination. The paper's own normal-mode calculation accompanies the table; the value here is the observed vapour figure, not the calculated one."
        },
        {
          "id": 292,
          "key": "Dinu.HowVibrationalNotations.2024",
