{
      "id": "meoh_ch3as",
      "species": "methanol",
      "group": "methanol_product",
      "vibration_modes": ["methanol_stretch_antisym"],
      "vibration": {
        "category": "stretch",
        "subtype": "asymmetric",
        "branch": null
      },
      "atoms": "H-C-H",
      "wn_start": 2905,
      "wn_end": 2980,
      "short": "νₐₛ(CH₂) MeOH",
      "description": "The antisymmetric stretch of methanol's two out-of-plane C-H bonds, a CH₂ motion because the in-plane hydrogen has no part in it. In the free molecule it is not one band but three, near 2967, 2928 and 2912 cm⁻¹: the fundamental is mixed with combinations of the methyl deformations and no observed band is dominated by it. Deuterating the methyl group collapses the pattern, which is how the mixing is demonstrated. Molecularly adsorbed methanol absorbs in the same window, 10 to 20 cm⁻¹ above methoxy, so gas and surface are carried here as one band. The width is that of the multiplet, not an uncertainty.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 294,
          "key": "Wu.BondingGeometryReactivity.2000",
          "medium": "vacuum",
          "form": "adsorbed",
          "wn": 2948,
          "measured_on": "tio2",
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": [
            "direct-dosing"
          ],
          "note": "Methanol dosed on TiO₂, so this is the adsorbed molecule and not the gas: it is removed by evacuation at 200 °C together with its νₛ(CH₃) partner, leaving methoxy on the surface. It sits inside the free molecule's own multiplet for this mode, which is why the two are carried as one band here. Measured after dosing 2 Torr of methanol and evacuating the cell (base pressure 1 × 10⁻⁷ Torr), the spectrum recorded at 35 °C."
        },
        {
          "id": 295,
          "key": "Furic.MethanolIsolatedMatrix.1993",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "laser_nm": 515,
          "wn": 2978,
          "technique": "raman",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Table 2, vapour column of a Raman study recording vapour, liquid and argon-matrix methanol on one instrument, 515 nm, 3 W at the sample for the vapour cell. Assigned there as ν₉, the CH₃ asymmetric stretch, and parenthesised, which marks it as the uncertain one of the set. The same table carries 2926 cm⁻¹ in the vapour as a combination and 2956 as the 2ν₄ overtone, so the paper already sees three features here without naming them a resonance."
        },
        {
          "id": 296,
          "key": "Falk.InfraredSpectraMethanol.1961",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "wn": 2973,
          "note": "Table I, CH₃OH vapour in a 10-cm cell at 80 mmHg and room temperature: 2973 cm⁻¹ (vs), with shoulders at 2982, 2934 and 2912. Falk treats the a′ and a″ asymmetric stretches as one unresolved envelope and notes in his own footnote that Fermi resonance with an overtone or combination of the methyl bends produces the extreme frequencies of the group. Later work (Serrallach 1974, Dinu 2024) makes that a three-component resonance rather than a single fundamental.",
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": []
        },
        {
          "id": 297,
          "key": "Dinu.HowVibrationalNotations.2024",
          "medium": "matrix",
          "form": "free",
          "wn": [2966.9, 2928.2, 2912.0],
          "note": "Table 3 and Fig. 7a: in solid neon at 6 K this mode is not one band but three, at 2966.9, 2928.2 and 2912.0 cm⁻¹ (2961.8, 2930.0 and 2914.2 in argon). The VCI analysis finds no state dominated by the ν₉ fundamental: 2966.9 cm⁻¹ is 59.9% the ν₄+ν₁₀ combination against 28.3% ν₉, and 2912.0 cm⁻¹ is best labelled ν₅+ν₁₀. Deuterating the methyl group collapses the pattern, which is how the resonance is demonstrated. Assigning a single band here to an asymmetric methyl stretch is the misassignment this paper exists to correct.",
          "technique": "transmission",
          "tags": ["isotope-labeling"]
        }
      ],
      "intensity": "s",
      "width": "broad",
      "confidence": "confirmed",
      "tags": ["undissociated", "misassignment-warning"]
    },
