      "short": "ν(CO) MeOH",
      "description": "Methanol C-O stretch (MeOH*/MeOH(g)). Falls in the 1000–1200 cm⁻¹ window shared with monodentate and bidentate methoxy ν(C-O); CH₃OH(a) and CH₃O(a) routinely coexist after low-temperature alcohol dosing and contribute jointly to this region. Disambiguate via the CH₃ stretching region: adsorbed methanol shows νₐₛ/νₛ blue-shifted by ~10–20 cm⁻¹ relative to methoxy.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 322,
          "key": "Furic.MethanolIsolatedMatrix.1993",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
