          ],
          "note": "Methanol dosed on TiO₂ at 35 °C, where CH₃OH* and CH₃O* coexist. The paper places both species' C-O stretches in the 1000–1200 cm⁻¹ region but resolves a position only for the methoxy pair (1045 and 1126 cm⁻¹), so no wavenumber is recorded for methanol here. Kept as a claim because the coexistence is the paper's own argument for why this region cannot be read as one species. Measured after dosing 2 Torr of methanol and evacuating the cell (base pressure 1 × 10⁻⁷ Torr), the spectrum recorded at 35 °C."
        },
        {
          "id": 325,
