      "description": "First overtone of the methanol C-O stretch, weak but sitting squarely in the window where CO on a reduced metal absorbs. Gas-phase methanol over a working catalyst therefore puts a band near 2056 cm⁻¹ that has nothing to do with adsorbed CO, with its R and P branches about 20 cm⁻¹ either side. Rotational structure is the discriminator: an adsorbed carbonyl has none. It moves with the C-O fundamental on deuteration, to about 1960 cm⁻¹ in the fully deuterated molecule.",
