      "short": "ν(OD) surface",
      "description": "A surface hydroxyl measured under D₂ or D₂O. The O-D stretch sits at about 1/1.36 of the O-H position, moving the hydroxyl region from 3400 to 3750 cm⁻¹ down into 2500 to 2750 cm⁻¹, where little else on an oxide absorbs. The pattern of components survives the shift, so it is the cleanest way to prove a band is a hydroxyl and to count how many kinds a surface carries. It overlaps the C-D stretches of deuterated adsorbates.",
