          "technique": "drifts",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Figs. 1 and S3 (in-situ DRIFTS, precipitated Ga₂O₃, 0.1 MPa D₂ at 450 °C): the deuteride pair, with the same shoulder-plus-main shape as the hydride pair and in the same intensity order, so 1442 cm⁻¹ pairs with 2011 cm⁻¹ and 1430 cm⁻¹ with 1988 cm⁻¹. The measured ν(Ga-H)/ν(Ga-D) ratio is 1.39 against 1.40 from the reduced masses. The paper does not assign the two deuteride components to the two Ga coordinations itself, so only the generic Ga centre is recorded here. A D₂ temperature-programmed surface reaction after CO₂ adsorption puts the band at 1429 cm⁻¹ (Fig. S14)."
