          "note": "Table 3 and Fig. 3B, 30 bar. CZ, a coprecipitated Cu/ZnO with Cu:Zn 2.1:1, diluted to 8 wt% in KBr and activated in H₂ at 513 K; 3H₂/CO₂ at 20 NmL min⁻¹, 513 K, 4 cm⁻¹, 64 scans. A small feature at 1691 cm⁻¹, tabulated as ν(C=O) of more strongly surface-bound formic acid or, with the authors’ own question mark, as ν(Zn-H); they cite 1660, 1707 and 1688/1678 cm⁻¹ from the literature for the hydride and none for the acid. One of four bands (1759, 1691, 1457 and 1398 cm⁻¹) whose intensity rises with the GHSV and with the methanol in the outlet gas, which is why the paper counts it among the true intermediates rather than the spectators. No isotope experiment is offered that would separate the two readings."
