      "short": "lattice overtones SiO₂",
      "description": "Not an adsorbate. Overtones and combinations of the Si-O-Si framework vibrations of silica itself, which absorbs so strongly in its fundamentals that little below about 1600 cm⁻¹ survives in diffuse reflectance. The clearest pair sits near 1870 and 1985 cm⁻¹, in the window of bridged and linear metal carbonyls; silicas and zeolites carry more of the series between 1400 and 2800 cm⁻¹. Their shape and position move with temperature and with rehydration, so a difference spectrum referenced to a background at another temperature grows peaks and valleys here that belong to neither spectrum and read convincingly as adsorbed CO. A background taken on the same sample at the same temperature and humidity removes them.",
