      "short": "lattice A₁(g) α-Al₂O₃",
      "description": "The strongest Raman line of corundum, α-Al₂O₃, and the lower of its two totally symmetric lattice modes. Corundum has two Al₂O₃ units in a rhombohedral cell of factor group D(3d), and of its optical phonons, 2A₁(g) + 2A₁(u) + 3A₂(g) + 2A₂(u) + 5E(g) + 4E(u), only the seven g modes 2A₁(g) + 5E(g) are Raman-active. The lattice is centrosymmetric, so none of them absorbs in the infrared, which sees the A₂(u) and E(u) modes instead. Like every corundum line it softens and broadens on heating, by about 11 cm⁻¹ up to 1080 °C, which makes it a Raman thermometer. The seven lines identify the α phase: γ- and η-Al₂O₃ show no Raman bands.",
