      "description": "A weak Raman line near 725 cm⁻¹ that a perfect corundum crystal does not have: it is none of the seven allowed lattice modes of α-Al₂O₃. It has been seen in synthetic sapphire where impurities and point defects concentrate, and attributed tentatively to a transition that iron or another 3d impurity makes allowed. Its presence beside the E(g) line at 750 cm⁻¹ therefore speaks to the purity of the crystal rather than to its phase.",
