          "note": "Fig. 2 (Sample 1, about 1 cm off the centre of the window; instrument as for the seven lattice lines): a subtle line at 724.6 cm⁻¹, present in every spectrum taken more than 1 cm from the centre and absent at it, where all lines are also weaker. The paper reads it, with the stronger lines above 640 cm⁻¹, as iron ions or other defects concentrated off-centre, and suggests unknown impurities activate the transition, most likely d-elements of the 4th period. A second new line at 176.3 cm⁻¹ it declines to interpret, possibly a laser plasma line. At the very edge, where the window touched the cryostat, only fluorescence remained, which the paper takes as a possible partial conversion of α- to γ-Al₂O₃ after two years at liquid-nitrogen temperature.",
