          "measured_on": "in2o3_c",
          "technique": "raman",
          "laser_nm": 532,
          "form": "lattice",
          "note": "Fig. 6 (room-temperature visible Raman, 532 nm, 7 mW, 5 s, normalized; cubic In₂O₃ from In(OH)₃ precipitated with NH₄OH, PDF 06-0416, beside Pd-P/In₂O₃ and Pd-I/In₂O₃): 364 cm⁻¹, assigned to ν(In-O-In). Its intensity grows markedly on Pd/In₂O₃, which the paper attributes in part to more oxygen vacancies, from breaking one of the double oxygen bridges In-O-In.",
          "tags": []
