      "symmetry": "E<sub>g</sub>",
      "short": "lattice E(g) anatase",
      "description": "The strongest Raman line of anatase TiO₂, the lowest of its three E(g) lattice modes. Anatase (I4₁/amd) has six Raman-active modes, A₁(g) + 2B₁(g) + 3E(g), and three infrared-active ones, A₂(u) + 2E(u); it is centrosymmetric, so none of its Raman lines absorbs in the infrared. This line is intense enough to reveal anatase at a few per cent. It nearly coincides with rutile's weak B₁(g) at 143 cm⁻¹, so in a mixture a line here is anatase. In nanocrystals it moves up by several wavenumbers and broadens.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
