          "form": "lattice",
          "note": "Table II and Fig. 2 (anatase: TiO₂ from slowly evaporated tetraisopropyl titanate, heated to 450 °C in air; powder in a capillary, back-scattering, 488 nm argon-ion line, 2 cm⁻¹ slit, room temperature): 147 cm⁻¹, the strongest band of the spectrum, assigned E(g) against the single-crystal data of Ohsaka et al. (144 cm⁻¹). The paper notes it falls almost on rutile's B₁(g) at 144.",
          "tags": []
        }
