          "form": "lattice",
          "note": "Table I and Fig. 1 (rutile: the same sol-gel TiO₂ heated to 750 °C in air for 5 h; powder in a capillary, back-scattering, 488 nm argon-ion line, 2 cm⁻¹ slit, room temperature): an anomalously strong, broad band at 235 cm⁻¹ with structure at high resolution, attributed to second-order or disorder-induced scattering. The paper weighs Narayanan's polarisation data, Porto's combination reading and Hara and Nicol's disorder reading, and leaves the choice open.",
          "tags": []
        }
