      "wn_end": 500,
      "short": "D1 ring mode SiO₂",
      "description": "The D1 defect line of amorphous silica, a sharp band near 490 cm⁻¹ above the network band. It is a breathing motion of the oxygens of small rings, almost pure oxygen motion, assigned to four-membered siloxane rings in the small planar ring model and to Si=O on paracrystalline surfaces in the cluster model. Its intensity reports the ring population, which sintering, crystallisation, oxygen and water change.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 517,
          "key": "Lee.SituRamanSpectroscopy.2008",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "lattice",
          "wn": 487,
          "measured_on": "sio2_fumed",
