          "laser_nm": 532,
          "note": "Section 3.2 and Fig. 2 (in-situ Raman, 532 nm, 10 mW; dehydrated 8% V₂O₅/SiO₂ on the same fumed silica at 450 °C, during H₂¹⁸O exchange), a band the paper attributes to the silica support: D1 at 487 cm⁻¹, attributed to tetracyclosiloxane (four-membered) rings, which does not appreciably shift with ¹⁸O.",
          "tags": []
        },
        {
          "id": 518,
          "key": "Ivanda.RamanSpectroscopySiO2.2003",
          "form": "lattice",
          "wn": 495,
          "measured_on": "sio2_glass",
          "technique": "raman",
          "note": "Introduction (polarised VV Raman, double monochromator with photomultiplier; silica glasses sintered from Degussa OX50 fumed silica, about 120 nm particles, 50 m² g⁻¹; spectra normalised to the amplitude at 440 cm⁻¹): D1 at 495 cm⁻¹, quoted from the literature (its ref. 2) rather than read off its own spectra; four-membered rings in the small planar ring model, double-bonded Si=O on the [100] surface of paracrystalline domains in the cluster model. Its amplitude falls with crystallisation and in water vapour and rises in oxygen and with hydrogen in the glass.",
          "tags": []
        },
        {
          "id": 531,
          "key": "Li.FiberglassScienceTechnology.2021",
          "form": "lattice",
