        "branch": "S"
      },
      "branch_group": "n2_stretch_branches",
      "atoms": "N-N",
      "wn_start": 2337,
      "wn_end": 2420,
      "short": "ν(NN) N₂",
      "description": "The S branch of the nitrogen stretch, ΔJ = +2, above the Q branch and the mirror of the O branch below it. Weak, and normally an unresolved tail: nitrogen's rotational constant is about 2 cm⁻¹, so its lines sit only a few wavenumbers apart and blur together at any ordinary resolution. The window is the envelope the populated levels reach rather than a reported position.",
      "based_on": [],
