          "note": "Fig. 5 and Fig. 8: the S branch of vibrational N₂, marked on the figure as the red-side tail of the Q branch, recorded in room-temperature air at 10 atm alongside the O branch to fix the polarizability ratio (a₀/b₀)² = 0.25. The paper prints no position for it, so none is recorded. In the simulated 30 atm spectra it overlaps the pure-rotational H₂ S(11) line. Spontaneous Raman with a pulsed Nd:YAG. The paper never states the line: 532 nm is inferred from its own figure axes, where the 2331 cm⁻¹ N₂ Q branch falls at about 607 nm.",
          "tags": []
        }
      ],
