      "atoms": "H-H",
      "wn_start": 4150,
      "wn_end": 4170,
      "short": "ν(HH) H₂",
      "description": "The Q branch of the hydrogen stretch, ΔJ = 0, near 4160 cm⁻¹ and the highest fundamental of any common molecule. H₂ is homonuclear and infrared-forbidden, so Raman is the only route to it. Its rotational constant is very large, about 59 cm⁻¹, which throws the O and S branches hundreds of wavenumbers clear of the centre instead of leaving them as tails: hydrogen's branches are separate features rather than wings on one band.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
