          "id": 357,
          "key": "Kojima.QuantitativeAnalysisSpectral.2005",
          "wn": 4160,
          "technique": "srs",
          "laser_nm": 532,
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "note": "Sect. 3.1 and Fig. 7: 4160 cm⁻¹ is the fundamental frequency the paper assigns to ν₀ for the vibrational-H₂ line-shape diagram, with an averaged line separation within the branch of 19.8 cm⁻¹, far smaller than the 180 cm⁻¹ separation of the pure-rotational spectrum. Measured in a 10 atm H₂-air flame at 1133 K, the temperature itself taken from the pure-rotational H₂ lines. The paper names only a pulsed Nd:YAG and never states the line; 532 nm is inferred from its own figure axes.",
          "tags": []
        }
      ],
      "intensity": "s",
      "width": "sharp",
      "confidence": "confirmed",
      "tags": ["ir-inactive"]
    },
