          "form": "free",
          "note": "Fig. 7 and Sect. 3.3.2: labelled O(0,3) in the paper's own O(v″,J″) form, where the 0 is the lower vibrational level and is implicit here. It is one of the five lines O(0,3) to O(0,7) drawn across 620 to 690 nm in a 10 atm H₂-air flame at 1133 K, the temperature taken from the pure-rotational H₂ lines. No wavenumber is printed: the text places the line around 657 nm, which is 3576 cm⁻¹ at the inferred 532 nm excitation. This is the line that falls inside the water stretching envelope, overlapping it by 18% at an equivalence ratio of 5.0 in the simulated 30 atm spectra. Spontaneous Raman with a pulsed Nd:YAG. The paper never states the line: 532 nm is inferred from its own figure axes, where the 2331 cm⁻¹ N₂ Q branch falls at about 607 nm.",
          "tags": []
        }
