      "description": "One line of the pure rotational Raman spectrum of hydrogen, the transition from J = 2 to J = 4. Nothing vibrates: the molecule only turns faster, and Raman reaches the change directly through the polarizability. Only ΔJ = +2 arises for pure rotation, since the upper level is by definition the higher one, so this spectrum is an S branch and nothing else. Hydrogen spreads it over more than 2000 cm⁻¹, with lines about 180 cm⁻¹ apart, which is why they are carried one by one.",
