      "atoms": "H-C-H",
      "wn_start": 2100,
      "wn_end": 2115,
      "short": "νₛ(DCD) CD₄",
      "description": "The totally symmetric stretch of methane-d₄, the deuterated twin of ν₁ in CH₄ and the strongest single feature of its Raman spectrum. Infrared-forbidden, as in the parent. Being totally symmetric it is the one methane band restricted to ΔJ = 0, so it is a bare Q branch with no rotational wings at all, which is what makes it so sharp against the branch structure of the other two fundamentals.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 385,
          "key": "Shepherd.RamanSpectrumMethaned4.1957",
          "wn": 2108,
          "technique": "raman",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Gaseous CD₄ at 1 atm, photographed on a grating spectrograph at 10.5 cm⁻¹ per mm with about 1 cm⁻¹ resolution, excited by the mercury arc (Hg 4047 and Hg 4078). A Q branch at 2107.8 cm⁻¹, called the strongest single feature of the spectrum and assigned here to ν₁, correcting MacWood and Urey, who had read this shift as 2ν₂ and placed ν₁ at 2084.7 cm⁻¹. The line is somewhat broadened, probably by a superimposed band tentatively assigned to the E component of 2ν₂ in Coriolis interaction with ν₃."
        }
      ],
      "intensity": "vs",
      "width": "sharp",
      "confidence": "confirmed",
      "tags": ["ir-inactive"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch4g_d4_bend_sym_o",
