      "wn_start": 964,
      "wn_end": 1076,
      "short": "δₛ(DCD) CD₄",
      "description": "The O branch of the doubly degenerate deformation of methane-d₄, the deuterated twin of ν₂ in CH₄. This is the band that settles what a spherical top shows in Raman: Placzek and Teller give ΔJ = 0, ±1, ±2 for a degenerate band of a spherical top, and all five branches are resolved and assigned here line by line. The window is the span of the assigned lines themselves, not an envelope computed from a rotational constant.",
      "based_on": [],
      "references": [
        {
          "id": 386,
          "key": "Shepherd.RamanSpectrumMethaned4.1957",
          "technique": "raman",
          "medium": "gas",
          "form": "free",
          "tags": [],
          "note": "Table I (gaseous CD₄ at 1 atm, Hg 4358, 10.5 cm⁻¹ per mm, about 1 cm⁻¹ resolution). O(2) at 1075.1 cm⁻¹ down to O(14) at 964.2, assigned line by line. With P below it this is the direct evidence that a spherical top reaches both ΔJ = −2 and −1 in one Raman band."
        }
      ],
      "intensity": "w",
      "width": "broad",
      "confidence": "confirmed",
      "tags": ["ir-inactive", "degenerated"]
